  "question": {
    "text": "An inductor of self inductance 1 H connected in series with a resistor of $100 \\pi \\mathrm{ohm}$ and an ac supply of $100 \\pi$ volt, 50 Hz. Maximum current flowing in the circuit is ________ A.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Impedance of circuit<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{Z}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\left(\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\left(\\omega_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right)^2} \\\\\n& =\\sqrt{(100 \\pi)^2+(2 \\pi \\times 50 \\times 1)^2} \\\\\n& =\\sqrt{(100 \\pi)^2+(100 \\pi)^2} \\\\\n& =\\sqrt{2} \\times 100 \\pi \\\\\n& \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\frac{V}{2}=\\frac{100 \\pi}{\\sqrt{2} \\times 100 \\pi}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{I}_{\\max }=\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\sqrt{2} \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\text { Ampere }<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Correct Answer : 1",
    "image": null
  },
